Xiaomi 6X (wayne) HyperOS 4 - OFFLINE EXPERIMENTAL PACKAGE

No physical device was available. Boot, encryption, radio, camera, fingerprint
and other hardware behavior have not been tested. Strict SELinux neverallow
checking still fails. This is not a verified stable release.

Supported prerequisite: wayne already using the Miku Android 15 retrofit
dynamic partition layout with metadata on system and system/vendor/cust backing
devices. This package does not convert a stock or other partition layout.

Download all ZIP parts and compare them to SHA256SUMS. Concatenate parts in
numeric order into one ZIP, then extract. Windows: use copy /b; Linux/macOS:
use cat. Do not extract or flash a single part on its own.

Python 3.11+ is required. Run python install.py --verify-only to check all
images without a device. The JSON manifest lists exact image hashes and status.

Installing writes system, vendor and boot. Back up your data and the original
images first. Enter a compatible fastbootd on an unlocked wayne and use current
Android platform-tools. Run python install.py --flash --serial DEVICE_SERIAL.
The script rejects a different device, unsupported layout and insufficient
space. It preserves existing product/system_ext allocations, writes no firmware,
does not erase userdata and does not reboot automatically. A data reset may be
necessary across Android versions, but is not performed by this package.

Static reports are in reports/. Their scope is limited: HAL declarations are
not proof that the services run; entry-point ELF symbol checks do not resolve
all linker namespaces or APEX behavior. Runtime SELinux compilation with -N
does not mean strict neverallow checking passed.

